.TH PUTC 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
putc \- write one byte to a stream
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <stdio.h>
.B int putc(int character, FILE *stream);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Writes the low byte to the Crunch stream, as
.BR fputc (3crunch).
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the written byte as an unsigned value, or EOF on error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fputc (3crunch)
